is that you don't wanna
start seeking this out.

00:32:07.890 --> 00:32:09.933
Because then, you're flirting with it,

00:32:10.950 --> 00:32:12.630
like demonic activity,

00:32:12.630 --> 00:32:15.540
as something that could be fun.

00:32:15.540 --> 00:32:16.470
It's the same reason

00:32:16.470 --> 00:32:19.230
that we were too old for "Harry Potter".

00:32:19.230 --> 00:32:21.600
But yeah, we were on the
fringes of that movement

00:32:21.600 --> 00:32:23.760
that was like, "If we were younger,

00:32:23.760 --> 00:32:25.950
our parents wouldn't have allowed us

00:32:25.950 --> 00:32:27.343
to read 'Harry Potter'."

00:32:27.343 --> 00:32:29.310
Because of the sorcery.

00:32:29.310 --> 00:32:31.890
And I think, my view was always,

00:32:31.890 --> 00:32:35.310
I think, that if Satan existed

00:32:35.310 --> 00:32:37.620
and at the time, I, definitely,
believed that he did,

00:32:37.620 --> 00:32:41.130
that he was super crafty and super smart.

00:32:41.130 --> 00:32:41.963
So, it would be like-

00:32:41.963 --> 00:32:42.796
Right.

00:32:42.796 --> 00:32:44.190
What's more strategic?

00:32:44.190 --> 00:32:46.920
And I would say, it's
more strategic for Satan

00:32:46.920 --> 00:32:50.580
to have some sort of subtle
influence over this professor

00:32:50.580 --> 00:32:52.680
that I'm going to this class

00:32:52.680 --> 00:32:57.390
and he is causing me
to doubt my worldview,

00:32:57.390 --> 00:33:00.300
he's causing me to doubt
the truth of Christianity,

00:33:00.300 --> 00:33:02.520
the legitimacy of the
resurrection or whatever,

00:33:02.520 --> 00:33:05.130
like, this religion professor
is saying these things

00:33:05.130 --> 00:33:06.990
that are challenging my worldview.

00:33:06.990 --> 00:33:09.300
That guy is under the influence of Satan.

00:33:09.300 --> 00:33:12.210
And Satan is gonna be much more impactful

00:33:12.210 --> 00:33:15.870
in the world at large if he's
working through academia.

00:33:15.870 --> 00:33:18.060
And so, you end up developing this view

00:33:18.060 --> 00:33:21.210
that the principalities and the powers

00:33:21.210 --> 00:33:23.340
of Satan and his minions,

00:33:23.340 --> 00:33:25.110
are not in the "Ouija" board

00:33:25.110 --> 00:33:27.180
that you can get off of
the shelf in "Walmart",

00:33:27.180 --> 00:33:28.653
they're in the classroom.

00:33:29.786 --> 00:33:30.619
Yep.

00:33:30.619 --> 00:33:32.250
They're in the places that we're debating

00:33:32.250 --> 00:33:33.573
and defining culture.

00:33:34.950 --> 00:33:36.360
Yeah, changing with the times.

00:33:36.360 --> 00:33:37.193
Right.

00:33:37.193 --> 00:33:39.783
And according to the old Rhett,

00:33:40.770 --> 00:33:43.230
the way that I changed,

00:33:43.230 --> 00:33:45.810
and this is very much the outspoken view

00:33:45.810 --> 00:33:47.820
of many people who talk about me and you

00:33:47.820 --> 00:33:49.980
and from the Christian world,

00:33:49.980 --> 00:33:52.290
is that we fell to the vices of Satan

00:33:52.290 --> 00:33:56.340
that we are, were and still
are under demonic influences

00:33:56.340 --> 00:33:58.350
and that's what's
guiding us at this point.

00:33:58.350 --> 00:33:59.183
Oh, wow!

00:33:59.183 --> 00:34:00.016
Yeah!

00:34:00.016 --> 00:34:00.849
Well, of course, what else-

00:34:00.849 --> 00:34:02.070
That's the scariest story ever.

00:34:02.070 --> 00:34:04.170
Well, what else could it be?

00:34:04.170 --> 00:34:07.440
Just somebody, learning that
it's, probably, not true?

00:34:07.440 --> 00:34:08.670
That doesn't make any sense.

00:34:08.670 --> 00:34:09.900
It couldn't just be that.

00:34:09.900 --> 00:34:10.740
There's, also, this,

00:34:10.740 --> 00:34:13.380
like, "Okay, what of
your own sinful nature

00:34:13.380 --> 00:34:18.090
and like, your selfish
in-most desires drive you?"

00:34:18.090 --> 00:34:19.043
So, it's like-

00:34:19.043 --> 00:34:20.310
Yeah, yeah, yeah, of course.

00:34:20.310 --> 00:34:21.143
You become your own God, yeah.

00:34:21.143 --> 00:34:25.050
Also, tended to own my faults as my own,

00:34:25.050 --> 00:34:28.290
more than, I would say, I
gave into the temptation

00:34:28.290 --> 00:34:31.110
of some external satanic force.

00:34:31.110 --> 00:34:34.050
Like, yeah, we could
have done it all our own

00:34:34.050 --> 00:34:35.880
without the influence of Satan.

00:34:35.880 --> 00:34:38.610
It just depends on what
your take is, I guess.

00:34:38.610 --> 00:34:39.720
Let's go back to ghost.

00:34:39.720 --> 00:34:41.220
Hi, my name's Ellie

00:34:41.220 --> 00:34:44.640
and I have a somewhat spooky story,

00:34:44.640 --> 00:34:46.503
per your "Twitter" request.

00:34:47.400 --> 00:34:50.220
My grandmother haunts my entire family,

00:34:50.220 --> 00:34:51.330
it's just a fact.

00:34:51.330 --> 00:34:54.030
It's not in any sort of scary way.

00:34:54.030 --> 00:34:56.830
She has a very distinct perfume smell

00:34:57.960 --> 00:35:00.330
and anytime, she wants to
make her presence known,

00:35:00.330 --> 00:35:02.280
we all smell it.

00:35:02.280 --> 00:35:06.480
It's come up when we're
all together for holidays,

00:35:06.480 --> 00:35:09.180
or I don't know, when
something big happens.

00:35:09.180 --> 00:35:10.560
It came up most recently for me,

00:35:10.560 --> 00:35:14.130
'cause I got a tattoo in her husband,

00:35:14.130 --> 00:35:16.170
my grandfather's handwriting.

00:35:16.170 --> 00:35:19.320
But yeah, it's more of
a comforting haunting.

00:35:19.320 --> 00:35:20.720
But nonetheless, a haunting.

00:35:21.630 --> 00:35:23.490
I hope, y'all have a great day.

00:35:23.490 --> 00:35:24.360
Bye.

00:35:24.360 --> 00:35:27.540
Well, that ain't gonna
happen, now, after that story,

00:35:27.540 --> 00:35:30.720
I'm not having a great
day with your grandma,

00:35:30.720 --> 00:35:32.190
just spraying perfume.

00:35:32.190 --> 00:35:34.860
Perfume gives me a headache.

00:35:34.860 --> 00:35:37.740
This is, probably, the scariest
story, I've heard today.

00:35:37.740 --> 00:35:38.573
But you don't know,

00:35:38.573 --> 00:35:40.380
if ghost perfume, that has
the same, sort of, impact.

00:35:40.380 --> 00:35:42.030
Grandma ghost perfume,

00:35:42.030 --> 00:35:44.850
is going to, like, make my brain hurt.

00:35:44.850 --> 00:35:46.110
I mean, Jenna,

00:35:46.110 --> 00:35:49.260
I mean, I don't know, if you ever think

00:35:49.260 --> 00:35:52.770
about the awkward conversation
we had about your perfume.

00:35:52.770 --> 00:35:54.067
But I think about it often.

00:35:55.410 --> 00:35:57.813
What do you remember
about that conversation?

00:35:59.100 --> 00:36:02.670
We were on tour in Toronto.

00:36:02.670 --> 00:36:04.336
Oh!

00:36:04.336 --> 00:36:05.169
Okay.

00:36:05.169 --> 00:36:06.690
It was a little overcast.

00:36:06.690 --> 00:36:07.523
I remember, exactly.

00:36:07.523 --> 00:36:10.560
We were walking back from,
like, a lunch, or a breakfast,

00:36:10.560 --> 00:36:11.393
back to the hotel

00:36:11.393 --> 00:36:14.850
before you had your
performances that night.

00:36:14.850 --> 00:36:19.402
And yeah, we were
walking along and it was-

00:36:19.402 --> 00:36:20.311
The three of us, maybe?

00:36:20.311 --> 00:36:21.144
The three of us,

00:36:21.144 --> 00:36:22.230
it was the three of us.

00:36:22.230 --> 00:36:24.540
And you were like, something about,

00:36:24.540 --> 00:36:25.950
I can't remember, exactly, how it started,

00:36:25.950 --> 00:36:27.307
but you were just, basically, like,

00:36:27.307 --> 00:36:29.730
"The perfume that you wear,

00:36:29.730 --> 00:36:32.419
sometimes, it gives me a headache."

00:36:32.419 --> 00:36:34.560
And I was like, "Okay."

00:36:34.560 --> 00:36:38.580
It was "Acqua Di Gioia", or something,

00:36:38.580 --> 00:36:39.549
I can never pronounce it.

00:36:39.549 --> 00:36:40.821
How committed were you to this perfume?

00:36:40.821 --> 00:36:42.853
Was this your scent?

00:36:42.853 --> 00:36:43.770
I wasn't fully committed.

00:36:43.770 --> 00:36:44.603
I mean, it was the only-

00:36:44.603 --> 00:36:45.436
If you died-

00:36:45.436 --> 00:36:46.391
Yeah.

00:36:46.391 --> 00:36:49.080
And your family wanted
to know your presence-

00:36:49.080 --> 00:36:50.610
It wasn't my signature scent.

00:36:50.610 --> 00:36:51.650
Would this be the scent that
you sprayed in the room?

00:36:51.650 --> 00:36:52.740
It wasn't your signature.

00:36:52.740 --> 00:36:54.090
Yeah, I still have it,

00:36:54.090 --> 00:36:56.259
but I don't wear it around you, anymore.

00:36:57.480 --> 00:36:58.800
But I've worn other perfumes

00:36:58.800 --> 00:37:02.730
and you haven't had
that same reaction, so.

00:37:02.730 --> 00:37:05.190
Because if you know, that
I would tell you if I did.

00:37:05.190 --> 00:37:06.023
Yes.

00:37:06.023 --> 00:37:07.620
If it did bother you,
just go ahead and tell me.

00:37:07.620 --> 00:37:09.300
But yeah, I did wear other perfume

00:37:09.300 --> 00:37:10.983
and you haven't made a comment.

00:37:14.070 --> 00:37:15.900
If our interactions are-

00:37:15.900 --> 00:37:17.163
it goes both ways.

00:37:18.090 --> 00:37:19.800
If they become defined by something

00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:22.890
that like, really, gives you a headache-

00:37:22.890 --> 00:37:23.872
Yeah.

00:37:23.872 --> 00:37:25.538
Or a toothache, or any type of ache.

00:37:25.538 --> 00:37:26.371
I would hope, that you would tell me,

00:37:26.371 --> 00:37:28.590
like, that's the communication climate

00:37:28.590 --> 00:37:31.740
that we have created by me,

00:37:31.740 --> 00:37:33.600
just in the nicest way possible,

00:37:33.600 --> 00:37:36.477
telling you, "Don't
wear perfume around me."

00:37:37.431 --> 00:37:38.264
Full stop.

00:37:38.264 --> 00:37:39.097
Full stop.

00:37:39.097 --> 00:37:39.930
I think, that the level of-

00:37:39.930 --> 00:37:41.940
I didn't know, you were wearing
other perfumes around me.

00:37:41.940 --> 00:37:44.670
I feel, kind of, betrayed.

00:37:44.670 --> 00:37:46.946
But you're pushing your-

00:37:46.946 --> 00:37:48.150
you know what?

00:37:48.150 --> 00:37:50.520
I thought I said, "No perfume."

00:37:50.520 --> 00:37:51.750
But I'm just joking, now.

00:37:51.750 --> 00:37:52.814
You said that one.

00:37:52.814 --> 00:37:53.940
You said that specific one.

00:37:53.940 --> 00:37:55.320
But that's not, really,
what I was thinking.

00:37:55.320 --> 00:37:56.153
I was thinking-

00:37:56.153 --> 00:37:57.480
He, only, accepts, like, lotions

00:37:57.480 --> 00:37:59.010
from "Bath &amp; Body Works"

00:37:59.010 --> 00:38:00.120
that smell like strawberries.

00:38:00.120 --> 00:38:01.350
Yeah, but you're right,

00:38:01.350 --> 00:38:02.880
you haven't given me a headache

00:38:02.880 --> 00:38:05.940
from the way that you've
smelled, since then.

00:38:05.940 --> 00:38:09.411
Just a headache from
how I talk to you guys?

00:38:09.411 --> 00:38:11.077
No.

00:38:11.077 --> 00:38:13.650
But I think, that the level
of perfume that you wear

00:38:13.650 --> 00:38:15.990
during your life,

00:38:15.990 --> 00:38:20.070
'cause some people,
really, go real, real hard

00:38:20.070 --> 00:38:21.900
with how much fragrance they put on.

00:38:21.900 --> 00:38:24.270
And maybe, if you have a very high level

00:38:24.270 --> 00:38:26.280
and there's a saturation in your skin,

00:38:26.280 --> 00:38:28.620
that can pass to the afterlife.

00:38:28.620 --> 00:38:30.210
And I believe, I met someone,

00:38:30.210 --> 00:38:31.860
who, this would be the case with,

00:38:33.390 --> 00:38:35.850
just this couple of days ago.

00:38:35.850 --> 00:38:40.470
I was going down to the
bottom of my driveway,

00:38:40.470 --> 00:38:44.400
which is a hill to bring
the trash cans back up

00:38:44.400 --> 00:38:45.933
to the top of the driveway.

00:38:46.800 --> 00:38:48.660
And there was a young couple

00:38:48.660 --> 00:38:50.580
that was getting into a car,

00:38:50.580 --> 00:38:52.440
coming out of someone's house

00:38:52.440 --> 00:38:56.820
and they got no closer than
50 feet, outside, okay?

00:39:05.300 --> 00:39:06.720
And it was not windy.

00:39:08.040 --> 00:39:09.903
And I smelled this woman,

00:39:11.340 --> 00:39:13.830
or I smelled this woman's perfume.

00:39:13.830 --> 00:39:14.760
It was so intense.

00:39:14.760 --> 00:39:17.493
And as I ascended my driveway,

00:39:18.630 --> 00:39:22.570
I was setting the trash cans down

00:39:23.940 --> 00:39:26.310
at the top of my driveway
and could still smell it.

00:39:26.310 --> 00:39:28.833
Well, you gotta clear that nasal passages,

00:39:29.700 --> 00:39:30.550
you gotta blow out hard.

00:39:30.550 --> 00:39:32.130
Well, the only point I'm making,

00:39:32.130 --> 00:39:35.220
is that, well, a, I just feel
like that's overdoing it.

00:39:35.220 --> 00:39:36.120
It's overdoing it.

00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:40.140
But b, when that woman becomes a ghost,

00:39:40.140 --> 00:39:41.460
she'll be a smelly ghost,

00:39:41.460 --> 00:39:43.110
like this grandma.
Do you think,

00:39:43.110 --> 00:39:45.960
this grandma, it's just she smells strong.

00:39:45.960 --> 00:39:48.390
You don't think, she's, like, spraying it

00:39:48.390 --> 00:39:49.980
and trying to communicate?

00:39:49.980 --> 00:39:51.270
Oh, you think it's ghost perfume

00:39:51.270 --> 00:39:53.370
that she's, like, coming in and tch, tch!

00:39:53.370 --> 00:39:55.020
Yeah, that's, kind of, how I was thinking.

00:39:55.020 --> 00:39:57.330
Well, I think, it somehow got through,

00:39:57.330 --> 00:39:58.163
it got through.

00:39:59.730 --> 00:40:02.070
I mean, some form of you gets through,

00:40:02.070 --> 00:40:04.680
some form of your physical form, right?

00:40:04.680 --> 00:40:06.090
The little girl was a little girl,

00:40:06.090 --> 00:40:08.850
the face didn't come,
the face was left behind.

00:40:08.850 --> 00:40:09.683
Yeah.

00:40:09.683 --> 00:40:10.640
She didn't get to bring her face.

00:40:10.640 --> 00:40:11.473
Right.

00:40:11.473 --> 00:40:12.480
Sometimes, things don't transfer.

00:40:12.480 --> 00:40:16.230
But I think, that if you've
saturated your epidermis

00:40:16.230 --> 00:40:17.700
with this smell,

00:40:17.700 --> 00:40:18.533
I think, that the people-

00:40:18.533 --> 00:40:20.192
It can cross over, so, to speak.

00:40:20.192 --> 00:40:21.025
The people, who make a decision

00:40:21.025 --> 00:40:22.950
about what's important to you,

00:40:22.950 --> 00:40:25.507
they're, like, looking at
the list and they're like

00:40:25.507 --> 00:40:27.690
"Smelling like this is
important to this lady.

00:40:27.690 --> 00:40:29.220
Let it through."

00:40:29.220 --> 00:40:30.053
I think, this is-

00:40:30.053 --> 00:40:30.886
They let the perfume through.

00:40:30.886 --> 00:40:32.250
This is a cool one, though, right?

00:40:32.250 --> 00:40:33.137
Cause it's like-

00:40:33.137 --> 00:40:34.262
Yeah.

00:40:34.262 --> 00:40:35.490
It's a happy haunting,

00:40:35.490 --> 00:40:38.403
like, "I'm still here,

00:40:41.130 --> 00:40:43.077
I haven't completely left."

00:40:43.920 --> 00:40:44.753
Yeah.

00:40:46.260 --> 00:40:48.240
It doesn't sound like
a rewarding experience

00:40:48.240 --> 00:40:49.680
for the grandma though, you know?

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:51.148
It's like-

00:40:51.148 --> 00:40:53.490
Well, you don't know what
it's like on the other side.

00:40:53.490 --> 00:40:55.620
Yeah, I, really, don't, Rhett.

00:40:55.620 --> 00:40:56.453
You don't know what it's like to-

00:40:56.453 --> 00:40:57.286
I really don't.

00:40:57.286 --> 00:40:59.490
To attend "Thanksgiving" as a ghost.

00:40:59.490 --> 00:41:01.380
I mean, it might be horrible.

00:41:01.380 --> 00:41:02.213
It might be like,

00:41:02.213 --> 00:41:04.137
"Man, I wish, I could
eat that Turkey leg."

00:41:05.070 --> 00:41:05.903
But it might be like,

00:41:05.903 --> 00:41:08.073
"I have no taste for Turkey any longer.

00:41:09.120 --> 00:41:11.940
It's just wonderful to see
my former family gather."

00:41:11.940 --> 00:41:12.885
All right.

00:41:12.885 --> 00:41:14.900
If this is where you're going,

00:41:14.900 --> 00:41:18.738
let's just go with one from
the not-as-creepy category,

00:41:18.738 --> 00:41:20.670
'cause I would like to break it up.

00:41:20.670 --> 00:41:22.601
Hey, Rhett and Link.

00:41:22.601 --> 00:41:23.820
So, my name is Jordan

00:41:23.820 --> 00:41:26.370
and I think, that you guys
might, really, like this one.

00:41:26.370 --> 00:41:29.730
Because I know, that you
guys are fans of "The Office"

00:41:29.730 --> 00:41:32.279
and mine, sort of, revolves around that.

00:41:32.279 --> 00:41:33.112
Okay.

00:41:33.112 --> 00:41:33.945
So, my spooky story,

00:41:33.945 --> 00:41:36.780
is that when I was about 13 or so,

00:41:36.780 --> 00:41:40.920
I went with my family to Scranton

00:41:40.920 --> 00:41:42.960
and we stayed at the Scranton Radisson

00:41:42.960 --> 00:41:45.180
and we just had a whole weekend

00:41:45.180 --> 00:41:47.130
where we visited all locations

00:41:47.130 --> 00:41:49.597
that they mentioned in "The Office".

00:41:49.597 --> 00:41:50.430
Really cool weekend,

00:41:50.430 --> 00:41:52.293
except, at the Scranton Radisson,

00:41:53.280 --> 00:41:57.510
apparently, there is a history
there of it being haunted

00:41:57.510 --> 00:41:58.710
and if you look up pictures,

00:41:58.710 --> 00:42:02.750
it definitely looks, kind
of, like, it's haunted.

00:42:06.270 --> 00:42:11.270
And so, I, then, got a
little scared once we staying

00:42:12.630 --> 00:42:14.730
and I realized that this
place is, probably, haunted

00:42:14.730 --> 00:42:16.920
and I looked it up and there were stories.

00:42:16.920 --> 00:42:19.380
And anyways, long story short,

00:42:19.380 --> 00:42:22.080
my mom is a medium and I asked her

00:42:22.080 --> 00:42:24.090
and she said, yeah, no,

00:42:24.090 --> 00:42:26.040
she, definitely, is
picking up on some things.

00:42:26.040 --> 00:42:28.350
So, all night, I was terrified

00:42:28.350 --> 00:42:30.877
and when I woke up, I was like,

00:42:30.877 --> 00:42:32.460
"Okay, cool, we did it.

00:42:32.460 --> 00:42:37.020
We got through the weekend
and there was no incidents."

00:42:37.020 --> 00:42:39.750
And then, of course, right
as I'm about to leave,

00:42:39.750 --> 00:42:42.390
I unplug my charger from the wall

00:42:42.390 --> 00:42:44.250
and I swear to you,

00:42:44.250 --> 00:42:48.000
my fingers were not
touching anything else.

00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:50.940
It was not touching the wall,
nothing was sticking out.

00:42:50.940 --> 00:42:52.830
When I unplugged it,

00:42:52.830 --> 00:42:57.180
my finger got cut and
really bad and was bleeding

00:42:57.180 --> 00:43:00.480
and it's, just, non-stop
